<title>USA: Mass. says to sell $700 mln of bonds shortly.</title>
<headline>Mass. says to sell $700 mln of bonds shortly.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts, taking advantage of the market's recent strength, plans to sell around $700 million of refunding and new money bonds &quot;within minutes,&quot; a state official said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Ken Olshansky, deputy treasurer, said that the negotiated offering will be divided between $500 million of refunding bonds and $200 million of new money bonds.</p>
</text>
